PLAIN WORDS (patch ignores this header; apply from the kit folder with:  patch -p1 < this file)
FIX 2: the long garden wall got no wall sheet and three other courtyard sheets sat on the wrong face, because earth runs under every wall so the 'nearest ground' hint is
undecided. A frames entry of the set file may now say  "front": {"<object name regex>": "-y" | "+x" | ... | "toward:X,Y", optionally "@N" for the plane}  (world directions).
Without it, a wall the old rule could not decide is tried again toward the set's first camera. Where the old rule found a front, nothing changes.
TESTED: the reader run on the street and the lockout file gives byte-identical pictures and arrays with and without this patch (14 of 15 pack files identical; manifest.json
differs only by timings and its 'made' time stamp). Courtyard: 3 sheets (one wall failed) -> 4 sheets, all facing the garden once the set file names the fronts
(see fix2 - courtyard set file).

